 sec('brief','Candidate brief',brief),sec('workflow','Run a bounded interview',`Scheduled ${meta.minutes} minutes. Use the Interview center to start ${interview.id}, or copy its AI interviewer instruction into a connected MCP client. Coaching mode permits requested hints; exam mode begins with this brief and lets you ask clarifying questions. The engine records hint use and supports pause/resume. Record actual diagrams, estimates and answers in the session notebook; do not rely on an AI chat transcript being visible automatically.

Suggested allocation: scope and facts5, initial reasoning15, detailed mechanism15, changed condition10, verification and summary10, reflection5. Ask the interviewer for one question at a time. Name your assumptions before using numbers, show a concrete operation history, and identify the authority that enforces each guarantee. It is acceptable to revise a decision when a new fact arrives; explain why the requirement changes its justification.`),sec('evidence','Submission and feedback contract',`Before finishing, save your final explanation and any unresolved questions. Finish closes the answering phase without inventing a grade. Without a connected model, use explicitly labeled self assessment against the weighted course rubric. With an AI evaluator, require exact supporting excerpts from candidate turns and targeted lesson references.

Judge the consistency of requirements, operation ordering, failure handling and tests. A polished diagram cannot compensate for acknowledging a result before the promised guarantee exists. After submission, compare your actual choices to the reference reasoning; alternatives may be defensible under different explicit assumptions. The score is educational evidence with uncertainty, not an assurance of a hiring outcome. Reattempt with the changed conditions after remediation, preserving the first attempt rather than overwriting history.`)
